spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:9:## Standing rules for every task
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:19:- **Planning decisions under D4 (owner-adjustable):** budget 
infrastructure fails closed — if a create, fence, or metrics budget cannot be checked, the request is refused as a 
transient 429 (the outbox retries it) instead of being allowed; Phase 4 keyed requests that carry no attempt 
generation keep the Phase 4 keyed contract (create, replay 200, 409) and take part in the same commit-time exclusion 
as fencing: such a request commits only if no fence state exists for its key at commit time, where fence state is 
created only by a fence call or a generation-carrying request (a generation-less create creates none, so Phase 4 
retries are unaffected); a generation-less request that loses to a fence stores nothing and is rejected as stale. 
Per-stream Realtime faults in E2E may inject Phoenix channel frames (`phx_error`, `phx_close`) or withhold a single 
topic's replies on the real socket; this counts as network shaping of a single stream (SPEC §15) — the real transport, 
joins, and application callbacks stay in place and no application health is set directly; a real server mechanism is 
preferred where one exists.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:21:## Observations grounding this plan (2026-10-06, corrected 
after review r1)
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:36:## T8 — Durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:37:Reasoning: The core of G1: write-before-dispatch, persistence 
across reload/close, ordered automatic drain meeting D1; unknown-outcome recovery follows in T27.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:38:Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user 
IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, reply target, requested mention IDs, original send time, window start, 
order, state, generation) before dispatch and before the composer clears; pending items render with a text label; 
items drain automatically per conversation in order when connectivity returns, with ≤ 10 pending and quota available 
all delivered within 10 s; confirmed items become the normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; 
attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, 
nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 message.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:39:Done when: AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, and AC-039 hold in 
the real UI, and 10 messages queued offline are delivered in order, once each, within 10 s of reconnecting.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:40:Verify by: New E2E specs for those ACs plus the 10-message D1 
timing case (offline context, reload offline, tab close, IndexedDB disabled and failing writes) pass 3 consecutive 
runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:41:Covers: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003, FR-010, FR-033, BR-002, BR-003, 
AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-011, AC-039
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:45:## T27 — Unknown-outcome recovery through the fence
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:47:Task: An attempt that ends without a usable response (network 
error after dispatch, timeout, 5xx after reaching the server, tab closed mid-request) leaves the item unknown; before 
any cancel, expiry, or redispatch the app fences it under a new generation; a stored result resolves as delivered 
(never cancelled or expired); a not-stored result only permits the transition that was requested — cancel and expiry 
complete without any create, and redispatch happens only while the item is still current, eligible, and inside its 
delivery window; cancel is offered only for items known not stored; a fence answered 403 `NOT_PARTICIPANT` (access 
lost while the item was unknown) makes the item failed per BR-005 with its text kept, stops automatic attempts, and is 
never treated as not stored (no expiry, no cancel) — "Tentar de novo" fences under a new generation first, so a stored 
result resolves as delivered and a not-stored result follows the normal rules, and "Apagar" only removes the local 
item.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:50:Covers: FR-005, FR-006, FR-009, BR-005, BR-007, AC-003, AC-038, 
AC-040, AC-042, AC-046
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:54:## T10 — Cross-tab outbox ownership and leases
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:55:Reasoning: Multi-tab exactly-once (R1-q16 B) is the riskiest 
client protocol; proven right after fenced recovery, before unrelated features.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:56:Task: All tabs of the same user share the outbox and show each 
item once; per conversation only the oldest unresolved item is eligible and one tab holds an atomic drain claim 
(lease: request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s) that ends on tab close/crash or expiry, after which another tab fences and 
resumes; when connectivity returns, an attempt started before or during the outage is superseded immediately under a 
new generation without waiting for the timeout or lease; no two create requests of one conversation overlap across 
tabs; cancel is atomic against claims and propagates to every tab.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:59:Covers: FR-002, FR-004, FR-005, BR-003, BR-007, AC-005, AC-006, 
AC-041, AC-045
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:63:## T9 — Definitive failures, rate-limit retry, and expiry
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:64:Reasoning: The user-visible failure states (BR-005 definitive, 
429 transient, BR-006 expiry) are a separate outcome from unknown recovery.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:65:Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text 
and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only later items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item 
proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under a new key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry 
automatically in order; items fenced as not stored 24 h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence 
answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not stored" — T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the 
original send time and opens a new 24 h window under the normal rules.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:66:Done when: AC-007, AC-008, AC-009 (drawer clause), AC-010, 
AC-043, and the AC-046 definitive-class clauses hold, and an expired item retried manually keeps its original send 
time in the outbox.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:67:Verify by: New E2E specs (removed room access via T24 re-add 
fixture, local quota exhaustion with 12 items, test-controlled clock for expiry, 409 key reuse, 403/400/413) pass 3 
consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge, with an outbox inspection for the preserved send time; regression suites pass.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:68:Covers: FR-002, FR-007, FR-008, FR-009, BR-005, BR-006, AC-007, 
AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-043, AC-046
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:72:## T11 — Identity fencing and session-end hold
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:81:## T12 — Sign-out confirmation with unsent messages
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:82:Reasoning: User-initiated sign-out deletes the outbox; touches 
the Presence logout path, so it is isolated.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:83:Task: At every reachable in-app sign-out control (today 
`EnhancedUserMenu`; any other found when the task starts is included), with N > 0 unsent items a dialog shows "Você 
tem N mensagens não enviadas. Sair apaga essas mensagens." with "Sair mesmo"/"Cancelar" (focus-trapped, Esc = 
Cancelar); Cancelar has no logout request, notice, or navigation; Sair mesmo stops drains in all tabs, deletes the 
user's outbox, and runs the existing sign-out with the Presence logout sequence unchanged; with N = 0 sign-out is 
unchanged.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:85:Verify by: New E2E spec (each reachable control enumerated in 
TRACK, a drain in flight in another tab, held responses after Sair mesmo, re-login with empty outbox, keyboard 
operation) passes 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; Presence E2E logout tests pass; presence-safety review 
recorded.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:90:## T13 — Realtime stream health, recovery, and connection banner
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:99:## T14 — Polling fallback during Realtime outages
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:108:## T15 — Reliable named members-only typing indicator
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:117:## T16 — Live cross-device unread, read state, and own messages
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:126:## T17 — @mention composition and rendering
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:128:Task: Typing "@" opens an accessible combobox/listbox of the 
conversation's current members (T4 roster) except the user, filtered while typing, operable by arrows/Enter/Tab/Esc 
and mouse; choosing inserts a highlighted mention whose user ID travels with the send — in the outbox item for text 
and in the create request for attachment/voice messages (including their Phase 4 retry); unselected "@name" text is 
plain; mentions render distinctly for everyone and the mentioned viewer sees the whole message highlighted with a 
non-color cue; a stale poll never drops a mention delivered by Realtime.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:135:## T18 — Mention desktop notifications
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:137:Task: With the Phase 4 toggle on and permission granted, a 
mentioned user gets one notification per message (DM, group, room, thread reply) titled "<Autor> mencionou você em 
<conversa>" with the full text, opening the conversation on click; emission is authorized with authoritative data 
under the current identity, then re-checked without further awaits for same signed-in user and no received removal 
signal; account switch or sign-out discards pending notifications; no tab notifies while any of the user's tabs in the 
browser is visible on that conversation; DM/group messages are never notified twice; an unchanged replay after a 
mentioned recipient left notifies no removed recipient.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:144:## T19 — Client messaging metrics that never affect messaging
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:146:Task: The client records send latency (from the original send 
time, including after a manual retry of an expired item), outbox wait, send outcomes by reason, every messaging 
stream's drops/recoveries/outage duration (messages, list, typing), and polling activations/duration in a bounded 
buffer (oldest dropped), delivering fire-and-forget batches (≤ 50 events, ≤ 16 KB, one in flight, aborted after 5 s, 
dropped under overload) to the T6 route; messaging never awaits metrics.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:148:Verify by: E2E spec producing the three episodes and an 
expired-item manual retry (test clock; controlled original-send and server-confirmation timestamps recorded; emitted 
latency equals their difference within 1 s, distinct from retry-to-confirm time) with a scan of raw T24 server log 
lines, plus failing, hanging, and flooded route runs asserting AC-001/AC-002 timing, ≤ 1 metrics request in flight, 5 
s abort, bounded buffer, no visible error; 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:153:## T20 — Drawer restore after reload, per user
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:162:## T21 — Old-build compatibility against the migrated local 
database
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:171:## T22 — Phase acceptance verification and final adversarial 
review
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:173:Task: On the final tree: messaging DB integration suite and 
the full messaging E2E suite (Phase 4 regression + every new spec) pass in Chrome and Edge; every new E2E spec has a 
recorded 3-consecutive-run pass in each; outbox, banner, typing, and mention flows are verified in Firefox and 
recorded; type-check, lint, and build pass; no unit test was added and every touched unit test is recorded as 
replaced; §13 accessibility points are checked; the whole work-item diff passes the adversarial review with every 
finding fixed or rejected with a reason.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:180:## T23 — Online migration rollout and owner acceptance
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:189:## Plan quality gate (version 4, 2026-10-07)
