Reasoning: G3's second half; depends on stream health and has its own merge-safety risk (AC-048).
Task: While any required stream has been unhealthy > 30 s and the tab is visible, the open conversation's new 
messages, its loaded messages' receipt summaries, any open reader-details list, and the conversation list are fetched 
every 15 s (immediately on becoming visible); none while hidden; no new poll once all streams are healthy; merges 
never duplicate messages or replace newer/enriched state or loaded history pages with older data.
Done when: AC-016 and the AC-048 reaction, receipt, attachment, and history-page clauses hold.
Verify by: New E2E specs (Realtime-only block with HTTP working, list-only outage, partial reads by C, hidden/visible, 
recovery during an in-flight poll with 60 s quiet check, held stale poll vs newer reaction/receipt/attachment message 
with older pages loaded) pass 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge; regression suites pass.
Covers: FR-016, BR-012, AC-016, AC-048
