  10 /**
  11  * Phase 5 T8 — durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery (FR-001,
  12  * FR-002, FR-003, FR-010, FR-033, BR-002, BR-003; AC-001, AC-002, AC-004,
  13  * AC-011, AC-039; D1, D2, D5).
  14  *
  15  * Everything is real: the app, its IndexedDB outbox, the create route and the
  16  * local database. Offline is the browser context's network emulation
  17  * (`context.setOffline`: navigator.onLine false, every request fails); held
  18  * creates are delayed pass-through to the real server (route.fetch). The
  19  * outbox is read from the page's own IndexedDB (inspection only). Storage
  20  * failures (AC-039) are browser conditions installed before the app loads:
  21  * `indexedDB.open` throwing SecurityError (storage blocked for the site), and
  22  * outbox write transactions that fail to commit (as on QuotaExceededError).
  23  * Chromium's CDP quota override does not affect IndexedDB in Playwright's
  24  * off-the-record contexts (probed in Chrome and Edge), so the write failure is
  25  * produced in the page instead.
  26  *
  27  * Exactly once is checked three ways: one stored row per text (any key) in
  28  * the database, at most one bubble per text in B's feed at any moment
  29  * (MutationObserver), and one stored bubble (no pending copy) in A's feed.
  30  */
  31 
  32 /** D1: with ≤ 10 pending and quota available, all delivered within 10 s of reconnecting. */
  33 const D1_DEADLINE_MS = 10_000;
  34 const STEP_TIMEOUT_MS = 20_000;
  35 const D5_TEXT = 'Este navegador não permite guardar mensagens; libere o armazenamento do site';
